INT. ESCAPE ROOM - "THE PHARAOH'S LAST BRUNCH" - NIGHT

A chamber made of cardboard and fabric: painted hieroglyphs, plastic jackals, a sarcophagus with a pizza box inside. A countdown clock on the wall reads 14:22.

Six coworkers are locked inside. BARRETT NWANKWO-HILL, thirties, wears a lanyard and an expression of dread. DOLORES FITZSIMMONS, fifties, has taken over the sarcophagus. YASMIN KARIMI-ODOM, twenties, holds a flashlight she doesn't need. GRIFFIN PELLERIN, forties, runs a finger down a wall of symbols. THEODOSIA "THEO" ABARA, thirties, checks her phone. And the intern, LEONARD VASQUEZ-TREMBLAY, nineteen, stands very still by the exit.

DOLORES
Okay. Everyone stop touching things.

BARRETT
I'm not touching anything.

GRIFFIN
You're touching the jackal.

BARRETT
The jackal touched me first.

YASMIN
Guys, there's a symbol that looks like a sandwich.

THEO
That's a hieroglyph for bread.

YASMIN
It looks like a sandwich.

DOLORES
Everyone, shut up, I'm thinking.

LEONARD
Mrs. Fitzsimmons, I think the pizza box is a clue.

DOLORES
Leonard, you're nineteen.

LEONARD
I'm aware.

GRIFFIN
Dolores, listen to the kid.

DOLORES
It's a pizza box. It's Pharaoh's brunch. It's a theme, Griffin.

THEO
Maybe it's both.

BARRETT
Both what?

THEO
A theme and a clue.

YASMIN
Can I open it?

DOLORES
No.

GRIFFIN
Yes.

BARRETT
Maybe.

LEONARD
(quietly)
I'm opening it.

He flips the lid. Inside the box lies a single slice of pepperoni and a folded note. They all gape.

LEONARD (CONT'D)
It says, "The first letter of every item you've touched."

BARRETT
Jackal.

GRIFFIN
Jar.

THEO
Jewel.

YASMIN
Scarab.

DOLORES
Sarcophagus.

LEONARD
Pizza.

BARRETT
J, J, J, S, S, P.

THEO
That doesn't spell anything.

GRIFFIN
Jjjsssp.

YASMIN
Maybe it's Egyptian.

DOLORES
It's not Egyptian, Yasmin, it's an acronym.

BARRETT
For what?

DOLORES
For "Jackals Should Stay Properly Put."

GRIFFIN
That's not a thing.

THEO
It could be a thing.

LEONARD
(whispering)
I think the clock is at four minutes.

They all turn. The clock reads 4:00. A silence follows, broken only by Yasmin's flashlight clicking on and off. Barrett sits on the floor and puts his head in his hands.

BARRETT
I told my wife I'd be home by nine.

GRIFFIN
You told her that?

BARRETT
I was optimistic.

DOLORES
Everyone, hands in. We're doing this together.

THEO
Doing what?

DOLORES
I have no idea. But we're doing it together.

They put their hands in a circle. Barrett lifts his head, wipes his eyes, and adds his own. Leonard, who has been watching the door the whole time, reaches out and presses a small button on the frame that reads, in tiny letters, EXIT.

The door clicks and swings open.

LEONARD
It was just a door.

Dolores glares. Griffin laughs. Theo lowers her phone. The clock keeps counting.

BARRETT
I'm going to need a minute.
